# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml`, the repository's third most conflicted path,
# because its step list was append-only. A gate lives here instead, so two
# branches adding gates create two files, never one shared region.
# `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --stage <stage>` runs them.
#
# The step-through debug session (issue #667, R383) names, for every stage of
# a turn, the Rust and JavaScript function that emits it. Both servers read
# those functions from data/meta/debug-stage-sources.lino, which
# scripts/generate-debug-stage-sources.mjs derives from the source tree (every
# function that appends a curated solver event kind). A new or moved append
# site committed without regenerating the table would leave the debugger
# naming code that no longer emits the stage, so this gate regenerates it and
# fails on any byte of drift. rust/tests/web/server-debug-session.test.mjs pins
# the same check and the exact emitters of a served `What is 2 + 2?` turn.
ci_gate check_debug_stage_sources
  stage web
  description "data/meta/debug-stage-sources.lino, the per-stage emitter table the debug session reads, is byte-current against the solver sources it is generated from."
  run "node scripts/generate-debug-stage-sources.mjs --check"
  justification "Issue #667 (R383) asked that each debugged stage name the code that emits it, derived from the source rather than a hand-kept table; a stale table would silently point the Rust and JavaScript panes at the wrong function."
